{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses returned.</b> On the morrow, on the third day of the month, which is the fourth day of the week — \"on the morrow, on the fourth day of the month, He said to Moses,\" etc., until \"he shall not come up with you.\" Immediately, \"and HaShem said to Moses: Behold, I come to you in the thickness of the cloud,\" etc., so that they would hear and believe in you that you are My emissary. But if they do not hear, they will say after some time: when You sent me to them, HaShem did not appear to you; even in you they will believe forever. On that very day, the fourth day of the month, in the portion of Mishpatim: \"And Moses came and told the people all the words of HaShem\" — that He said: \"Behold, I come to you in the thickness of the cloud,\" etc., until \"they will believe forever.\" And all the ordinances that were given at Marah, as it is written there: \"There He made for him a statute and an ordinance,\" \"and all the people answered with one voice and said: All that HaShem has spoken we will do.\" Immediately here, in the portion of Yitro: \"And Moses told the words of the people to HaShem\" — that they said: \"All the words that HaShem has spoken we will do.\" Here Rashi commented: \"A response to this matter — I have heard from them,\" etc. From where did Rashi say so? Rather, from the response of HaKadosh Baruch Hu, who said: \"for on the third day HaShem will descend\" — you learn that they sought to hear from His mouth. And from the fact that it is written \"before the eyes of all the people,\" you learn that they said: our wish is to see our King. On that very day itself, the fourth day of the month, it was said: \"And HaShem said to Moses: Go to the people and sanctify them,\" etc. Since it says thus, \"Go to the people and sanctify them today,\" etc., until \"do not approach a woman\" — the fourth and fifth days of the month, which are the fifth and sixth days of the week. \"And sanctify them\" — that they wash in water, and the proof is \"his garments shall be washed\", as it is written: \"and if he does not wash, his flesh shall not be washed\"; and thereby they will be holy. A parallel: \"and she is purified of her impurity\"; and through this they will be ready and pure from a woman — one learns the implicit from what is explicit."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:50.731736046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}